## Notifications (`notify` feature)

The kit emits events and posts each to the webhooks that subscribe to it:
`service.started` after the bind, `update.installed`, `update.ok`,
`update.failed`, `update.rolled_back`, `update.held`, and
`health.degraded` / `health.recovered` once per transition. {{ name }} may
add events of its own.

Webhooks are declared in the config file, one table per target:

```toml
[[notify.webhook]]
events = ["update.*", "health.degraded"]
url = "https://hooks.example.lan/{{ name }}"
headers = { "Authorization" = "Bearer ${{ '{' }}{{ prefix }}_HOOK_TOKEN}" }
```

`${VAR}` in a URL or header is read from the environment when the service
starts, so a secret stays out of the file. Delivery retries with backoff
and never blocks a request.
{%- endif %}

