## The smoke test the kit ships

`tests/kit_smoke.rs` comes from the kit and `chassis sync` keeps it current:
it starts {{ name }} on a free port with a temporary state directory, logs
in as the admin, issues a client, calls one API route with that client's
token and opens the dashboard. It is the fastest way to see whether a
change broke the kit's own path through this service, and it runs with the
project's own `cargo test`.

Do not edit it; write your own tests beside it. The harness it uses
(`chassis::testing`) is documented in the kit's `docs/TESTING.md`.
